    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a message in a bottle. Draw it as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate pieces laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every piece at the size it has in image 1 and lying level the way it lies in image 1 (if they do not all fit, draw them all a little smaller, at the same scale as each other).\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no piece touching or overlapping another:\n1. the green glass bottle exactly as in image 1, straight, lying level, neck to the right, but EMPTY: no note and nothing else inside it, just the clear green glass with its shine, and WITHOUT its cork: the neck open at its lip.\n2. the cork alone, whole: the top that shows in image 1 and its lower end that goes into the neck, drawn too, lying level as in image 1.\n3. the rolled paper note alone, tied round the middle with string, exactly as it looks inside the bottle in image 1: the same size, lying level, the same colours as seen through the green glass.\n\nEvery piece is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another piece, with its edges clean and smooth. It is an object, not a character: no face, no eyes, no mouth. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the pieces beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows, no water, no sand, no splashes or drops. Fully transparent background."
    }
